-- title:
--   Centre of the exceptional valuation on the blow-up chart
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, and $M'$ a nonzero natural number divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and suppose some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ carries $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((X))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H$ is the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, $\xi$ in the image of $A$, and uniformiser $\varpi$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$; let $j\in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((X))$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=qu$ for some unit $u$. Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $y\subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal containing $\varpi$ which is supersingular, in the sense that every homomorphism from $C$ onto an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y$ sends `jChartFin A K j` into [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7) (those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point). Let $J$ be an ideal of $C$ and $B$ the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$, and let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$, subject to: (R1) $C\subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; (R2) $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; (R3) $W\cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, $\mathfrak m_W=(\varpi)$, $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, $W$ is centred on $y$ (for $b\in C$, $b\in y$ iff its image lies in $\mathfrak m_W$), and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m_W\cap B$. Assume finally that the ideal $yB$ of $B$ generated by the image of $y$ is prime. Then an element of $B$ lies in $\mathfrak m_W$ if and only if it lies in $yB$; and for every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ whose contraction to $C$ is $y$, every element of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ lies in $Q$.
--
--   This identifies the centre $\mathfrak m_W\cap B$ of the exceptional valuation on the blow-up chart with the extension $yB$ of the supersingular maximal ideal, and shows it to be the least prime of $B$ above $y$ containing the uniformiser. It is used in the analysis of the Drinfeld fibre of the blow-up chart, in the comparison of decomposition and inertia for level automorphisms there, and in the identification of the exceptional valuation with the centre of the $uv$-crossing model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_mem_span_image_of_blowupChart_exceptionalValuation_of_isPrime.lean

